CHUNK({"chunk":"V","module":"m6","topics":[{"id":"m6-indian-acts","title":"Indian environmental Acts and Rules","short":"Indian Acts & Rules","blurb":"Every Indian Act and Rule in the syllabus with its year, what triggered it, what it set up and why it matters in the exam.","source":"Collected from Lectures W2–W4 (Water, Air, Noise, Solid waste, EPA, Forest and Wildlife Acts)","tabs":[{"title":"Quick table","html":"\n          <p class=\"lead\">Learn these as <b>year + one-line purpose + body it created</b>. Most MCQs ask \"which Act / which year / which body\".</p>\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Act / Rule</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><b>1972</b></td><td>Wildlife (Protection) Act</td><td>Protects wild animals, birds and plants through <b>Schedules</b> (Schedule I = highest protection); bans hunting of scheduled species; creates sanctuaries and national parks. India's domestic tool for <b>CITES</b>. Protects the <b>inhabitants</b>.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1974</b> (enacted 23 March 1974)</td><td>Water (Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act</td><td>India's <b>first comprehensive pollution law</b>. Set up the <b>CPCB (Section 3)</b> and <b>SPCBs (Section 4)</b>; consent needed before discharging effluent (Sections 24–26). Amended 1988 (stronger penalties).</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1980</b></td><td>Forest (Conservation) Act</td><td><b>Section 2</b>: no non-forest use of forest land without <b>prior Central Government approval</b>; took the power away from states; compensatory afforestation (CAMPA). Protects the <b>habitat</b>. Amended 1988, 1992, 2023.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1981</b></td><td>Air (Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act</td><td>Gave the CPCB/SPCBs power over <b>air</b> pollution; declares air pollution control areas. Inspired by the 1972 Stockholm Conference. <b>1987 amendment added noise</b> as an air pollutant.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1986</b> (passed 19 Nov 1986)</td><td>Environment (Protection) Act (EPA)</td><td><b>Umbrella law</b>: lets the Centre make rules and standards for <b>all</b> parts of the environment. Direct response to the <b>Bhopal Gas Tragedy (1984)</b> + Stockholm (1972).</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2000</b></td><td>Noise Pollution (Regulation and Control) Rules</td><td>Ambient noise limits for industrial, commercial, residential and silence zones; loudspeaker limits at night. Made under the EPA 1986.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2002</b></td><td>Biological Diversity Act</td><td>Implements the <b>CBD (1992)</b> in India: conservation, sustainable use and <b>fair sharing of benefits</b> from biological resources (National Biodiversity Authority).</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2010</b></td><td>National Green Tribunal (NGT) Act</td><td>Set up the <b>NGT</b>, a specialised fast-track court for environment cases; appeals under the Water Act (Section 33B) go to it.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2016</b></td><td>Solid Waste Management Rules</td><td>Made <b>segregation at source</b> mandatory (wet, dry, hazardous); duties on generators and local bodies.</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n          <div class=\"note exam\">Order to remember: <b>Wildlife 72 → Water 74 → Forest 80 → Air 81 → EPA 86</b>. Water came first, so <b>the Water Act created the CPCB</b>, and the Air Act reused it.</div>\n        "},{"title":"Why each matters","html":"\n          <ul>\n            <li><b>Wildlife Act 1972 + Forest Act 1980</b> are the <b>two-shield system</b>: Forest Act guards the habitat, Wildlife Act guards the animals and plants in it.</li>\n            <li><b>Water Act 1974</b> is the base of India's pollution-control system: CPCB at the national level, SPCBs in each state, the consent system, and penalties.</li>\n            <li><b>Air Act 1981</b> extended the same boards to air; the <b>1987 amendment</b> brought noise in.</li>\n            <li><b>EPA 1986</b> filled the gaps: one law for everything the earlier Acts missed (hazardous chemicals, industrial safety). Most later Rules (Noise 2000, SWM 2016) are made under it.</li>\n            <li><b>Biological Diversity Act 2002</b> is about <b>sustainable use and benefit sharing</b>, unlike the Wildlife Act which is about protection.</li>\n          </ul>\n          <div class=\"note exam\">Trap MCQ: \"Which Act is called the umbrella Act?\" → <b>EPA 1986</b>. \"Which Act established CPCB?\" → <b>Water Act 1974</b>. \"Which Act took forest diversion power from states?\" → <b>Forest (Conservation) Act 1980</b>.</div>\n        "},{"title":"Amendments & judgments","html":"\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td>1987</td><td>Air Act amended: <b>noise</b> added as an air pollutant.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>1988</td><td>Water Act amended: penalties increased, boards' powers strengthened. Forest Act amended the same year.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>1992</td><td>Forest (Conservation) Act amendment: allowed limited, selected developmental activities with approval.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>1996</td><td><b>T.N. Godavarman judgment</b> (Supreme Court): \"forest\" means any forest in the <b>dictionary sense</b>, whatever its ownership or record. Hugely widened the Forest Act.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2023</td><td>Forest (Conservation) Amendment Act: renamed and narrowed coverage to recorded forests (coverage clarified to start from October 1980); a current, debated issue.</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        "}],"flashcards":[{"front":"Which Act created the CPCB and SPCBs?","back":"<b>Water (Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1974</b> (Sections 3 and 4)."},{"front":"Which Act is the \"umbrella\" environmental law?","back":"<b>Environment (Protection) Act, 1986</b>."},{"front":"Which disaster triggered the EPA 1986?","back":"<b>Bhopal Gas Tragedy</b>, 2–3 December 1984 (MIC leak)."}],"cardCount":6,"formulaCount":0},{"id":"m6-international","title":"International conventions, protocols and summits","short":"International treaties","blurb":"Stockholm to Paris: every global agreement in the syllabus with its year, place and purpose.","source":"Collected from Lectures W2–W5 (Biodiversity, Chemical hazards, Kyoto, Paris, SDGs, Climate change)","tabs":[{"title":"Quick table","html":"\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Agreement / Summit</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><b>1971</b></td><td>Ramsar Convention (Ramsar, Iran)</td><td>Protects <b>wetlands</b> of international importance. India has 75+ Ramsar sites (e.g. Chilika Lake, Keoladeo).</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1972</b></td><td>Stockholm Conference (UN Conference on the Human Environment)</td><td><b>First major global summit</b> on the environment. Led to UNEP; triggered India's Water, Air and EPA Acts. 5 June became World Environment Day.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1973</b> (in force 1975)</td><td>CITES</td><td>Controls <b>international trade</b> in endangered species. Secretariat: Geneva. India joined 1976.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1987</b></td><td>Montreal Protocol</td><td>Phased out <b>CFCs</b> and other ozone-depleting substances. The most successful environmental treaty.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1987</b></td><td>Brundtland Report (\"Our Common Future\")</td><td>Defined <b>sustainable development</b>: meeting present needs without compromising future generations.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1988 / 1990</b></td><td>IPCC formed / First Assessment Report</td><td>Scientific basis that triggered the UNFCCC.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1992</b></td><td>Rio Earth Summit</td><td>Produced <b>UNFCCC</b>, <b>CBD</b> (Convention on Biological Diversity) and <b>Agenda 21</b>.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1997</b> (adopted 11 Dec; in force 16 Feb 2005)</td><td>Kyoto Protocol (COP3)</td><td><b>First binding emission cuts</b>, for developed (Annex I) countries only. Period 1: 2008–2012. Mechanisms: CDM, JI, emissions trading. India ratified Aug 2002.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2002</b></td><td>Johannesburg World Summit on Sustainable Development (Rio+10)</td><td>Renewed commitment; Johannesburg Plan of Implementation.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2009</b></td><td>Copenhagen (COP15)</td><td>Failed to give a binding treaty, but began voluntary pledges.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2012</b></td><td>Doha Amendment (COP18) &amp; Rio+20</td><td>Kyoto second period to 2020; Rio+20 outcome \"The Future We Want\" started the SDG process.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2013</b></td><td>Minamata Convention</td><td>Global treaty on <b>mercury</b> (named after Minamata disease, 1956).</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2015</b> (adopted Dec, COP21; in force 4 Nov 2016)</td><td>Paris Agreement</td><td>196 parties; keep warming <b>well below 2 °C, aim for 1.5 °C</b>; every country submits <b>NDCs</b>; global stocktake every 5 years.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2015</b></td><td>Sustainable Development Goals</td><td><b>17 SDGs</b> for 2030 (e.g. SDG 6 clean water, SDG 13 climate action).</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2022 / 2023</td><td>COP27 / COP28 (Dubai)</td><td>COP27 agreed a <b>loss and damage</b> fund, operationalised at COP28; COP28 finished the first global stocktake.</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n          <div class=\"note exam\">Pairs examiners love: <b>Montreal → ozone (CFCs)</b>, <b>Kyoto → binding GHG cuts</b>, <b>Paris → NDCs, 1.5 °C</b>, <b>Minamata → mercury</b>, <b>Ramsar → wetlands</b>, <b>CITES → wildlife trade</b>, <b>CBD → biodiversity</b>.</div>\n        "},{"title":"Kyoto vs Paris","html":"\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <thead><tr><th></th><th>Kyoto Protocol 1997</th><th>Paris Agreement 2015</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td>Who must cut</td><td>Only developed (Annex I) countries</td><td>All countries</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>Targets</td><td>Binding, set top-down</td><td>Self-set NDCs, bottom-up</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>Goal</td><td>~5% below 1990 levels (2008–12)</td><td>Well below 2 °C, aim 1.5 °C</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>In force</td><td>16 Feb 2005</td><td>4 Nov 2016</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>Weakness</td><td>US never ratified; big emitters (China, India) had no targets</td><td>NDCs not legally enforceable; US left 2020, rejoined 2021</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        "}],"flashcards":[{"front":"Montreal Protocol (1987) deals with?","back":"Phasing out <b>ozone-depleting substances</b> such as CFCs."},{"front":"Kyoto Protocol year and key feature?","back":"<b>1997</b> (COP3): first <b>binding</b> GHG cuts, developed countries only; in force 16 Feb 2005."},{"front":"Paris Agreement goal?","back":"<b>2015</b> (COP21): well below 2 °C, aim for 1.5 °C, through NDCs."}],"cardCount":6,"formulaCount":0},{"id":"m6-events-programmes","title":"Disasters, movements and government programmes","short":"Events & programmes","blurb":"The landmark disasters, case studies and Indian missions that the lectures attach dates to.","source":"Collected from Lectures W1–W5","tabs":[{"title":"Disasters & case studies","html":"\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Event</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td>1952</td><td>London Great Smog</td><td>Thousands died; led to the UK <b>Clean Air Act 1956</b>.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>1956</td><td>Minamata disease, Japan</td><td><b>Mercury</b> in fish from factory waste; led to the Minamata Convention 2013.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>1967</td><td>Koynanagar earthquake</td><td>Linked to the Koyna dam reservoir (reservoir-induced seismicity).</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>1973–1983</td><td>Silent Valley (Kerala)</td><td>Hydro project halted in 1983 after protests; declared a <b>national park</b>.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2–3 Dec 1984</td><td><b>Bhopal Gas Tragedy</b></td><td><b>Methyl isocyanate (MIC)</b> leak from Union Carbide plant; worst industrial disaster; triggered the <b>EPA 1986</b>.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>1989</td><td>Exxon Valdez oil spill</td><td>~41 million litres of oil off Alaska.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2005</td><td>Hurricane Katrina</td><td>Disaster management case study.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2010</td><td>Deepwater Horizon oil spill; Pakistan floods</td><td>Largest marine oil spill; one of the worst floods.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2013</td><td>Kedarnath landslide/flood</td><td>Triggered by intense rainfall; Himalayan disaster case.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2019</td><td>Cyclone Fani</td><td>Odisha's early-warning evacuation success.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>11 Mar 2020</td><td>COVID-19 declared a pandemic</td><td>Biological hazard case study (SARS-CoV-2).</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        "},{"title":"Indian programmes","html":"\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Programme</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td>1936</td><td>Jim Corbett National Park</td><td>India's <b>first national park</b> (Uttarakhand).</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>1973</td><td><b>Project Tiger</b></td><td>Tiger conservation via tiger reserves; one of India's biggest successes.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>1992</td><td><b>Project Elephant</b></td><td>Conserve elephants, habitats and corridors.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>1987, 2012</td><td>National Water Policy</td><td>Water planning; 2012 version stresses water as an economic good and efficiency.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2002</td><td>Bt cotton approved</td><td>India's GM crop case study.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2008</td><td>NAPCC</td><td>National Action Plan on Climate Change: <b>8 national missions</b> (e.g. Solar Mission).</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2014 / 2015</td><td>NMCG / <b>Namami Gange</b></td><td>Clean and rejuvenate the Ganga.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2019</td><td><b>NCAP</b></td><td>National Clean Air Programme: 20–30% cut in PM by 2024 (later 40% by 2026) in non-attainment cities.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2020</td><td><b>BS-VI</b></td><td>India jumped from BS-IV straight to BS-VI vehicle emission norms.</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n          <div class=\"note\">Important days: <b>22 April</b> Earth Day · <b>5 June</b> World Environment Day · <b>16 September</b> World Ozone Day (Montreal Protocol) · <b>22 March</b> World Water Day · <b>22 May</b> Biodiversity Day.</div>\n        "}],"flashcards":[{"front":"Gas in the Bhopal tragedy?","back":"<b>Methyl isocyanate (MIC)</b>, Union Carbide plant, 1984."},{"front":"Project Tiger began in?","back":"<b>1973</b>."},{"front":"Project Elephant began in?","back":"<b>1992</b>."}],"cardCount":5,"formulaCount":0},{"id":"m6-timeline","title":"Master timeline: the dates that matter","short":"Master timeline","blurb":"The dates worth learning, by topic and in order, with the low-yield ones cut.","source":"Compiled from the other three topics of this section","dates":[["London Great Smog",1952],["Minamata disease identified",1956],["Ramsar Convention (wetlands)",1971],["Stockholm Conference",1972],["Wildlife (Protection) Act",1972],["CITES signed",1973],["Project Tiger",1973],["Water (Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act",1974],["Forest (Conservation) Act",1980],["Air (Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act",1981],["Silent Valley project halted",1983],["Bhopal Gas Tragedy",1984],["Environment (Protection) Act",1986],["Montreal Protocol",1987],["Brundtland Report",1987],["Air Act amended to add noise",1987],["Rio Earth Summit (UNFCCC, CBD)",1992],["Project Elephant",1992],["Kyoto Protocol adopted",1997],["Noise Pollution (Regulation and Control) Rules",2000],["Biological Diversity Act",2002],["Kyoto Protocol entered into force",2005],["NAPCC (8 missions)",2008],["National Green Tribunal set up",2010],["Minamata Convention",2013],["Paris Agreement adopted",2015],["SDGs adopted",2015],["Solid Waste Management Rules",2016],["NCAP",2019]],"tabs":[{"title":"Must know (in order)","html":"\n          <p class=\"lead\">The <b>19 years to learn first</b>, oldest to newest. Short on time? Learn this tab. The topic tabs after it add the second-tier dates.</p>\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>What</th><th>Topic</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><b>1956</b></td><td>Minamata disease (mercury)</td><td>Disaster</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1971</b></td><td>Ramsar Convention (wetlands)</td><td>Global</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1972</b></td><td><b>Stockholm Conference</b> + <b>Wildlife (Protection) Act</b></td><td>Global / India law</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1973</b></td><td>CITES (wildlife trade) + <b>Project Tiger</b></td><td>Global / Programme</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1974</b></td><td><b>Water Act</b> &rarr; CPCB &amp; SPCBs</td><td>India law</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1980</b></td><td><b>Forest (Conservation) Act</b></td><td>India law</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1981</b></td><td><b>Air Act</b></td><td>India law</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1984</b></td><td><b>Bhopal Gas Tragedy</b> (MIC)</td><td>Disaster</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1986</b></td><td><b>Environment (Protection) Act</b>, the umbrella law</td><td>India law</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1987</b></td><td><b>Montreal Protocol</b> (ozone) + Brundtland Report + noise added to Air Act</td><td>Global / India law</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1992</b></td><td><b>Rio Earth Summit</b> (UNFCCC, CBD, Agenda 21) + Project Elephant</td><td>Global / Programme</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1997</b></td><td><b>Kyoto Protocol</b> (COP3)</td><td>Climate</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2002</b></td><td><b>Biological Diversity Act</b></td><td>India law</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2008</b></td><td>NAPCC (8 missions)</td><td>Programme</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2010</b></td><td><b>National Green Tribunal</b></td><td>India law</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2013</b></td><td><b>Minamata Convention</b> (mercury)</td><td>Global</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2015</b></td><td><b>Paris Agreement</b> (COP21) + <b>17 SDGs</b></td><td>Climate / Global</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2016</b></td><td><b>SWM Rules</b> (segregation at source)</td><td>India law</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2019</b></td><td><b>NCAP</b> (clean air)</td><td>Programme</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        "},{"title":"How to remember","html":"\n          <p class=\"lead\">Don't learn 30 years one by one. Learn a few <b>anchor years</b>, then hang everything else on them as \"+2\", \"+10\" or \"same year\".</p>\n          <h3>1. The five Indian Acts: \"Wild Water, Forest Air, Everything\"</h3>\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <thead><tr><th>Say</th><th>Act</th><th>Year</th><th>Hook</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><b>Wild</b></td><td>Wildlife</td><td>1972</td><td>Same year as <b>Stockholm</b>: India acted the year the world met.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Water</b></td><td>Water</td><td>1974</td><td>Stockholm <b>+2</b>. Water came first, so it created the <b>CPCB</b>.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Forest</b></td><td>Forest</td><td>1980</td><td>Start of the 80s. Forests first...</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Air</b></td><td>Air</td><td>1981</td><td>...then the air they clean, <b>one year later</b>.</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>Everything</b></td><td>EPA (umbrella)</td><td>1986</td><td>Bhopal 1984 <b>+2</b>. \"Everything\" = the umbrella law.</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n          <div class=\"note exam\">Pattern: <b>72, 74</b> (two years apart) then <b>80, 81</b> (back to back) then <b>86</b>. Acts are 70s–80s; <b>Rules</b> (Noise 2000, SWM 2016) come in the 2000s.</div>\n          <h3>2. The \"+2\" and \"+10\" chains</h3>\n          <ul>\n            <li><b>Stockholm 1972 → Water Act 1974</b> (+2).</li>\n            <li><b>Bhopal 1984 → EPA 1986</b> (+2) <b>→ noise added to Air Act 1987</b> (+1).</li>\n            <li><b>Montreal 1987 → Kyoto 1997</b> (+10): ozone, then climate.</li>\n            <li><b>CBD 1992 → Biological Diversity Act 2002</b> (+10): India's law for the Rio treaty.</li>\n            <li><b>Kyoto adopted 1997 → in force 2005</b> (8 years); <b>Paris adopted 2015 → in force 2016</b> (just 1 year).</li>\n          </ul>\n          <h3>3. \"Same year\" pairs</h3>\n          <ul>\n            <li><b>1956</b>: Minamata disease <b>and</b> the UK Clean Air Act.</li>\n            <li><b>1972</b>: Stockholm <b>and</b> the Wildlife Act.</li>\n            <li><b>1987</b>: Montreal Protocol, Brundtland Report, Air Act noise amendment.</li>\n            <li><b>1992</b>: Rio (UNFCCC + CBD + Agenda 21) <b>and</b> Project Elephant.</li>\n            <li><b>2015</b>: Paris Agreement <b>and</b> the 17 SDGs.</li>\n          </ul>\n          <h3>4. Small hooks</h3>\n          <ul>\n            <li><b>Project Tiger 1973</b> = Wildlife Act <b>+1</b>.</li>\n            <li><b>Minamata Convention 2013</b> is named after the 1956 mercury disease; both are about <b>mercury</b>.</li>\n            <li><b>NGT 2010</b>: round number, the \"green court of the new decade\".</li>\n            <li><b>BS-VI 2020</b>: \"<b>six</b> in twenty-twenty\" (India skipped BS-V).</li>\n            <li><b>Ramsar 1971</b> is the <b>oldest</b> treaty in the syllabus: \"wetlands first\".</li>\n          </ul>\n          <div class=\"note\">Then use the <b>date drill</b> at the top of the Laws, Acts &amp; dates page until you can answer 20 in a row.</div>\n        "},{"title":"Indian laws","html":"\n          <p class=\"lead\">Oldest to newest. <b>&#9733; bold</b> = must know; plain = good to know.</p>\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>What</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><b>1972</b></td><td>&#9733; Wildlife (Protection) Act: Schedules, protects the <b>inhabitants</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1974</b></td><td>&#9733; Water Act: created the <b>CPCB &amp; SPCBs</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1980</b></td><td>&#9733; Forest (Conservation) Act: Centre approval, protects the <b>habitat</b></td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1981</b></td><td>&#9733; Air Act: same boards, now for air</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1986</b></td><td>&#9733; Environment (Protection) Act: <b>umbrella law</b>, after Bhopal</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1987</b></td><td>&#9733; Air Act amended: <b>noise</b> added</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>1996</td><td>Godavarman judgment: \"forest\" in the dictionary sense</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2000</td><td>Noise Pollution Rules (made under the EPA)</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2002</b></td><td>&#9733; Biological Diversity Act: India's law for the CBD</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2010</b></td><td>&#9733; National Green Tribunal Act</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2016</b></td><td>&#9733; Solid Waste Management Rules: segregation at source</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2023</td><td>Forest (Conservation) Amendment Act</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        "},{"title":"Global treaties","html":"\n          <p class=\"lead\">Oldest to newest. <b>&#9733; bold</b> = must know; plain = good to know.</p>\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>What</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><b>1971</b></td><td>&#9733; Ramsar Convention: wetlands</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1972</b></td><td>&#9733; Stockholm Conference: first global summit, UNEP, 5 June</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1973</b></td><td>&#9733; CITES: trade in endangered species</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1987</b></td><td>&#9733; Montreal Protocol: ozone / CFCs</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1987</b></td><td>&#9733; Brundtland Report: defined sustainable development</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1992</b></td><td>&#9733; Rio Earth Summit: UNFCCC, CBD, Agenda 21</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1997</b></td><td>&#9733; Kyoto Protocol adopted: binding cuts, developed countries only</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2005</td><td>Kyoto enters into force (16 Feb)</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2013</b></td><td>&#9733; Minamata Convention: mercury</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2015</b></td><td>&#9733; Paris Agreement (COP21): 1.5 &deg;C, NDCs</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2015</b></td><td>&#9733; 17 SDGs for 2030</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2016</td><td>Paris enters into force (4 Nov)</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        "},{"title":"Disasters","html":"\n          <p class=\"lead\">Oldest to newest. <b>&#9733; bold</b> = must know; plain = good to know.</p>\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>What</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td>1952</td><td>London Great Smog &rarr; UK Clean Air Act 1956</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1956</b></td><td>&#9733; Minamata disease: mercury in fish</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>1983</td><td>Silent Valley hydro project halted</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1984</b></td><td>&#9733; Bhopal Gas Tragedy: MIC, Union Carbide &rarr; EPA 1986</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        "},{"title":"Programmes & days","html":"\n          <p class=\"lead\">Oldest to newest. <b>&#9733; bold</b> = must know; plain = good to know.</p>\n          <table class=\"tbl\">\n            <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>What</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><b>1936</b></td><td>&#9733; Jim Corbett: India's first national park</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1973</b></td><td>&#9733; Project Tiger</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>1992</b></td><td>&#9733; Project Elephant</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2008</b></td><td>&#9733; NAPCC: 8 national missions</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2015</td><td>Namami Gange</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><b>2019</b></td><td>&#9733; NCAP: cut PM in non-attainment cities</td></tr>\n              <tr><td>2020</td><td>BS-VI norms (skipped BS-V)</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n          <div class=\"note\">Days, in calendar order: <b>22 Mar</b> Water &middot; <b>22 Apr</b> Earth &middot; <b>22 May</b> Biodiversity (three 22nds) &middot; <b>5 Jun</b> Environment &middot; <b>16 Sep</b> Ozone.</div>\n          <h3>Skipped on purpose</h3>\n          <p>These dates appear in the lectures but are rarely asked, so they are left off this timeline and the date drill: Koyna 1967, Exxon Valdez 1989, Katrina 2005, Deepwater Horizon and Pakistan floods 2010, Kedarnath 2013, Fani 2019, COVID-19 2020, IPCC 1988, Johannesburg 2002, Copenhagen 2009, Doha / Rio+20 2012, COP27&ndash;28, the 1988 and 1992 Act amendments, National Water Policy, Bt cotton. Know what the <b>event</b> was; don't learn its year.</p>\n        "}],"flashcards":[{"front":"Order the five big Indian Acts.","back":"Wildlife 1972 → Water 1974 → Forest 1980 → Air 1981 → EPA 1986."},{"front":"Order the climate treaties.","back":"UNFCCC 1992 → Kyoto 1997 → Paris 2015."},{"front":"Which happened in 1987?","back":"Montreal Protocol, Brundtland Report, Air Act amendment (noise)."}],"cardCount":4,"formulaCount":0}]});
